nker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** in `src/money.py`, the comment on `round_money` says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That's why `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **The fix:** on a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed one line to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** run `ci-0001` passed on that commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool returned \"Unknown advisory FIN-212.\" The fix matches what the test and the code comment both say.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}